[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) merged every date report by subject. Read by cause, the 412 reports
hold three problems. Only the first has a fix.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem has its own ticket in the
[public repo](https://github.com/nagasai-mala/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues).
</Callout>

## What the reports say

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table files the 5 one-day reports under `parser`, because it goes by tenant. Counted by what the
reports say, `parser` is 374, `hint` is 33 and the one-day shift is 5. Together that is 412.

## The problems

1. **parser: 374 reports.** The shared parser reads dates month first; day-first tenants get them
   flipped. Fixed in `fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`
   ([issue 1](https://github.com/nagasai-mala/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/1)).
2. **hint: 33 reports.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field, so
   day-first tenants (alder.physio, copper.studio, pale.harbour) type month first. The parser fix
   does not touch this. The form is retired and the ticket is closed as won't fix, so these
   reports have no open ticket
   ([issue 2](https://github.com/nagasai-mala/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/2)).
3. **one-day shift: 5 reports.** R-41202, R-41209, R-41236, R-41344 and R-41620 describe a day off
   by one, not a month and day swapped. It looks like a timezone problem and needs its own look
   ([issue 3](https://github.com/nagasai-mala/mega-s01e03-what-it-shows/issues/3)).

## Why the desk missed it

Intake tags a report from the reporter's browser, which is a guess. The cause depends on the
tenant's locale and booking form. Subject matching ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
merged all three into one ticket.

